"Hardware-aware local model advice, runtime management, and chat\n\nUsage: rigspark [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]\n\nCommands:\n  recommend  Detect hardware and rank local models (default command)\n  can-run    Check whether this machine can run a model\n  plan       Show every execution path (GPU, multi-GPU, offload, CPU) for one model\n  up         Install verified weights and start a loopback server\n  switch     Switch the active model without moving memory\n  down       Stop owned servers or detach and forget an attached daemon without stopping it\n  ls         List active server state from local state (not installed-model inventory)\n  doctor     Diagnose hardware, runtimes, ports, and state\n  catalog    Show the model catalog or preview a catalog refresh\n  chat       Chat interactively, from piped input, or with one message\n  migrate    Copy or move memory between models\n  gui        Launch the loopback browser GUI\n  generate   Generate an image or video locally through ComfyUI\n\nOptions:\n      --json\n          Emit machine-readable JSON\n\n      --context <CONTEXT>\n          Context size in tokens (integer in 1..10000000)\n\n      --max-context\n          Report the largest context each model can hold\n\n      --context-percent <CONTEXT_PERCENT>\n          Use 25, 50, 75, or 100 percent of each model's context\n\n      --task <TASK>\n          Boost models for a task: chat, code, vision, reasoning, tools, embedding\n\n      --backend <BACKEND>\n          Runtime: ollama, llamacpp, mlx, lmstudio\n\n      --port <PORT>\n          Ollama port for --installed (default: 11434)\n\n      --installed\n          Inspect models installed in a local Ollama daemon\n\n      --fits-only\n          Only show installed models with known full-context fit\n\n      --available-backends\n          Only show models an installed backend can serve\n\n      --hardware <HARDWARE>\n          Evaluate a hardware profile JSON file instead of this machine\n\n      --catalog-path <CATALOG_PATH>\n          Load a catalog from this JSON file\n\n  -v, --version\n          Print version\n          \n          [alias: -V]\n\n      --perf-path <PERF_PATH>\n          Load throughput data from this JSON file\n\n      --kv-cache <KV_CACHE>\n          Size the KV cache as f16 (default), q8_0, or q4_0; needs a context flag\n          \n          [possible values: f16, q8_0, q4_0]\n\n  -h, --help\n          Print help\n\nWith no command, runs recommend. Use rigspark <command> --help for command options.\n"